    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i5ccoll",
      "content": "A person cannot see distant objects clearly. The defect and its correction are:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pl8kig0",
      "content": "A) Hypermetropia – Convex lens"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dyrqzds",
      "content": "B) Myopia – Concave lens"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "v84ts9z",
      "content": "C) Presbyopia – Bifocal lens"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "736gpqs",
      "content": "D) Astigmatism – Cylindrical lens"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "267yprf",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (Myopia – Concave lens)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "glp84ul",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "khhs74b",
      "content": "• If a person cannot see distant objects clearly, the image forms before the retina."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7lv6a4q",
      "content": "• This defect is called Myopia (short-sightedness)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fbdtbyh",
      "content": "• It is corrected using a concave lens which diverges the light rays."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jyvayk8",
      "content": "• Concave lens shifts the image back onto the retina."
    },
    {
      "id": "gfxe5k9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x6rz20k",
      "content": "The far point of a myopic person is 2 m. The power of corrective lens required is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mhi42up",
      "content": "A) -0.5 D"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7p5c63w",
      "content": "B) +0.5 D"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ww7m8v6",
      "content": "C) -2 D"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3wkj11o",
      "content": "D) +2 D"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wpo903f",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: A (-0.5 D)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8oqqhm9",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jpaogvs",
      "content": "For myopia, image of distant object should be formed at far point (2 m)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z6gi2sh",
      "content": "Object at infinity ⇒ u = -∞"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gc1658i",
      "content": "Image distance v = -2 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4wjk6yq",
      "content": "Using lens formula simplified for infinity:"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "MCQs",
      "id": "l7kzfww"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "c40ty4m",
      "content": "1/f = 1/v"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qeiprhw",
      "content": "1/f = -1/2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ix2r16b",
      "content": "f = -2 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d8e2fj8",
      "content": "Power P = 1/f = -1/2 = -0.5 D"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6fuop37",
      "content": "Negative sign confirms concave lens."
    },
    {
      "id": "cbikxfc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rpurji7",
      "content": "The blue colour of the sky is due to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gjuw5vr",
      "content": "A) Reflection"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fu1csgb",
      "content": "B) Refraction"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "b7ikosz",
      "content": "C) Scattering of light"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o1jzbn5",
      "content": "D) Dispersion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0hu493c",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (Scattering of light)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fiw4wko",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xkqb4zm",
      "content": "• Sunlight contains all colours."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b766w10",
      "content": "• Blue light has shorter wavelength."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ank68sq",
      "content": "• According to Rayleigh scattering, intensity ∝ 1/λ⁴."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7uc5qoy",
      "content": "• Hence blue light scatters more in atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "efe389z",
      "content": "• Therefore sky appears blue."
    },
    {
      "id": "r35r4ry",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n201fvc",
      "content": "Stars appear to twinkle due to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pu2q31a",
      "content": "A) Dispersion"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hv48qwp",
      "content": "B) Reflection"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hopv1ua",
      "content": "C) Atmospheric refraction"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "f4n2ss9",
      "content": "D) Interference"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "iwlbcpz",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (Atmospheric refraction)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b6fldi0",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bojqg44",
      "content": "• Light from stars passes through different layers of atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b52sj4x",
      "content": "• Atmospheric density continuously changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pnx7uv7",
      "content": "• This causes continuous refraction of light."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f9vmhmd",
      "content": "• Stars are point sources → brightness fluctuates → twinkling."
    },
